course: dictionary
lesson: 9622
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists each meaning with a number, and the sentence tells you which one to choose. «Stub your toe and there is a strange gap» is about hitting your foot on something hard, but a «ticket stub» is a small piece of paper you keep.
explain: The words around the word are your clues. If you see «ticket» or «pencil» next to stub, think about what is left over. A stub is the short end that remains after most of something has been used, or the small part you keep as a record.
explain: Stub can also be a doing word, as in «stub your toe». Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: A stub is the short end left after most of something has been used, like a pencil stub or a candle stub.
fact: A ticket stub is the small part of a ticket you keep as a record that you paid.
fact: To stub your toe means to hit it by accident against something hard.
fact: «Stub your toe and there is a strange gap»: first comes a bump, then a moment later the ache arrives.
fact: In computing, a stub is a short, unfinished piece of writing or code.
exercise: «I found a pencil stub in my pocket.» What is a stub here? | A paper ticket for the bus | A pocket for pencils | A long, sharp new pencil | *The short end left after most of the pencil was used
exercise: «Ella kept the ticket stub so she could prove she had paid.» What is a ticket stub? | A long train ride | *The small part of a ticket kept as a record | A cake with icing on top | A toe that has been hurt
exercise: «I stubbed my toe on the bed and yelled.» What does stubbed mean? | Wrapped in a warm blanket | Stayed in bed all day | *Hit by accident against something hard | Kicked a ball very gently
test: «Ben wrote a short, unfinished piece of code.» Which meaning of stub fits here? | *A short, unfinished piece of writing or code | Pain in the toe | Something used up at the end | A ticket record
test: Oscar says, «Stub only means one thing.» What is the best answer? | Yes, it only means a sore toe | *No, stub has several meanings, and the sentence shows which one | Yes, it only means a ticket | No, it means happy
exam: Which phrase means hitting your foot by accident against something hard? | Pencil stub | *Stub your toe | Ticket stub | Stub out
